body:
I just hit this issue myself with the same version of Godot. For reference, [here's a working C# playground](https://dotnetfiddle.net/yaJ7So) indicating that this should be fine in C# itself:

```cs
using System;

public class Program
{
	public static void Main()
	{
		Console.WriteLine("Hello World");
	}
}

public class BaseClass {
	public virtual long BuildCost {get; set;}
}

public class DerivedClass : BaseClass {
	public override long BuildCost { get => 500; }
}
```

I don't really know how this works under the hood, but if you just add an empty setter `set { }` to the overridden property, it builds properly, so in the OP's attached code, it should be this:

```cs
public override bool TestVar {
    get { return false; }
    set { } // extra empty setter
}
```

I can confirm, I have the exact same issue on 4.6.3.stable.mono.

> Parent class:
> public virtual ItemResource Resource { get; private set; }
> public virtual ItemResource NextResource { get; private set; }

> Childclass:
> public override ItemResource Resource => LeftVariant.Resource;
> 
>  public override ItemResource NextResource => LeftVariant.NextResource;
